{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=========================================================================\nHANDOFF UPDATE — J1 LANDED AND CLOSED before the pause completed.\nSupersedes the 'Immediate next actions' in the handoff block above.\n=========================================================================\n\nJ1 acb2 is DONE. Sequence completed after that block was written:\n  * CI run 30463387830 -> SUCCESS.\n  * Gerrit change 1009 earned BOTH gates: LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot) and\n    Verified +1 (rebar CI bot), 0 unresolved comments.\n  * SUBMITTED -> status MERGED at 2026-07-29 15:20:13. It landed FAST-FORWARD, so\n    gerrit/main is now exactly 7fc96b277 — my worktree HEAD already IS the merged state.\n    NOTE: origin (the GitHub mirror) had NOT replicated yet at pause time, so\n    'git merge --ff-only origin/main' said 'Already up to date' and a grep of origin/main\n    for the ticket found nothing. Confirmed via 'git fetch gerrit main' instead\n    (1bed2f0cd..7fc96b277). Do not mistake mirror lag for a failed submit.\n  * CLOSED J1: rebar transition acb2 in_progress closed -> 'UNBLOCKED: 62d9'.\n    J1 now carries BOTH attestations: plan-review + completion-verifier.\n  * Also fixed: the earlier 'rebar claim --assignee' calls reported success but stored an\n    EMPTY assignee on both the epic and J1. Set explicitly with 'rebar edit <id>\n    --assignee RebarBotNava'. WORTH CHECKING after any future claim.\n\n## CURRENT READY SET (rebar ready --epic e369): 62d9 (J2) and c97f (J5)\n\nNext actions for the new session, in order:\n\n1. J2 62d9 is NOW plan-reviewable (J1 closed). Run 'rebar review-plan 62d9-9f6d-ecf4-4743'.\n   Expect it to take ~18-22 min. Its description was heavily rewritten this session and\n   carries a detailed comment listing the three defects fixed — READ BOTH before implementing.\n   Record J1's merged Gerrit number (1009) on J2 before pushing it (epic AC8).\n2. J5 c97f is claimable in parallel RIGHT NOW — already plan-review PASSED and certified.\n3. Then J3 aac8 + J4 0a94 unblock once J2 closes; J6 needs J4+J5; J7 needs J3+J6; J8 needs J7.\n\nBoard: epic e369 in_progress (assignee RebarBotNava, plan review PASSED/certified);\nJ1 CLOSED; J2/J3/J4/J5/J6/J7/J8 open; bug fe15 open (discovered_from J1).\nWorktree /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family @ 7fc96b277 == gerrit/main, clean.\n========================================================================="},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338678644929001,"uuid":"84ed067b-70a9-4e73-93d1-09e881c2d259"}